## SQ-TN-12 | chain cap: five TNT going off in one tick fly at most 32 shrapnel pieces
@group A
@commands Five primed TNT summoned in one tick 20 blocks up at X 2100 (open air, so no piece stops on a block at once); count `creativecompat:shrapnel` while the pieces fly
@pass every count reads 32 or fewer; at least one count above 24 (more than one burst fired, so the cap was what held it)
@fails a count above 32: `ShrapnelSpawner` does not count the pieces in flight (`maxNearby`), or the config holds another value; every count 24 or fewer: only the first burst fired (look for a second explosion) or the count ran after the pieces were gone (timing)
> forceload add 2084 -16 2116 16
> kill @e[x=2084,y=-64,z=-16,dx=32,dy=60,dz=32,type=!minecraft:player]
> summon minecraft:armor_stand 2100.5 -40 0.5 {NoGravity:1b,Invisible:1b,Tags:["tn12"]}
> summon minecraft:armor_stand 2100.5 -40 0.5 {NoGravity:1b,Invisible:1b,Tags:["tn12"]}
> summon minecraft:armor_stand 2100.5 -40 0.5 {NoGravity:1b,Invisible:1b,Tags:["tn12"]}
> summon minecraft:armor_stand 2100.5 -40 0.5 {NoGravity:1b,Invisible:1b,Tags:["tn12"]}
> summon minecraft:armor_stand 2100.5 -40 0.5 {NoGravity:1b,Invisible:1b,Tags:["tn12"]}
sleep 1
> execute as @e[type=minecraft:armor_stand,tag=tn12] at @s run summon minecraft:tnt ~ ~ ~ {Fuse:4}
sleep 0.3
> execute if entity @e[type=creativecompat:shrapnel]
sleep 0.05
> execute if entity @e[type=creativecompat:shrapnel]
sleep 0.05
> execute if entity @e[type=creativecompat:shrapnel]
reject Test passed, count: (3[3-9]|[4-9]\d|\d{3,})$
count Test passed, count: (2[5-9]|3[0-2])$ >= 1
> kill @e[x=2084,y=-64,z=-16,dx=32,dy=60,dz=32,type=!minecraft:player]
